{"book":5,"chapter":25,"context":{"chapter":25,"title":"Fair Measures, a Brother's Name","summary":"Laws limit beatings to forty stripes, protect the working ox, provide for a dead brother's widow, and require honest weights. Israel is told to remember what Amalek did.","background":"A man was expected to marry his dead brother's childless widow so the dead man's name and land would continue; this 'levirate' custom (from Latin levir, brother-in-law) lies behind the stories of Tamar (Genesis 38) and Ruth. Paul uses verse 4 to argue that those who serve should be supported.","customs":[{"term":"Forty stripes","verses":"25:3","note":"A beating was capped at forty blows. Later Jewish practice stopped at thirty-nine to be safe (2 Corinthians 11:24)."},{"term":"Loosing the shoe","verses":"25:9-10","note":"If the brother refused, the widow pulled off his sandal and spat before the elders, publicly shaming his refusal."},{"term":"Divers weights","verses":"25:13-15","note":"Merchants weighed goods against stones carried in a bag. A cheat kept a heavy set for buying and a light set for selling."}],"watchFor":["'Lest... thy brother should seem vile unto thee' (v. 3).","Amalek attacked 'all that were feeble behind thee' (v. 18; Exodus 17:8-16)."],"connections":["1 Corinthians 9:9","2 Corinthians 11:24","Ruth 4:7-10","Exodus 17:8-16"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["כִּי","ki-","H3588","HTc","if"],["יִהְיֶה","yihyeh","H1961","HVqi3ms","it will happen"],["רִיב","riv","H7379","HNcmsa","a dispute"],["בֵּין","bein","H996","HAcmsc","between"],["אֲנָשִׁים","'anashim","H582","HNcmpa","people"],["וְנִגְּשׁוּ","venigeshu","H5066","Hc/VNq3cp","and they will draw near"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["הַמִּשְׁפָּט","hamishpat","H4941","HTd/Ncmsa","the place of judgment"],["וּשְׁפָטוּם","ushefatum","H8199","Hc/Vqq3cp/Sp3mp","and they will judge them"],["וְהִצְדִּיקוּ","vehitzdiku","H6663","Hc/Vhq3cp","and they will declare righteous"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הַצַּדִּיק","hatzadik","